{
 "about": "Round 69: two resource attributes compared under == and under !=: lists in another order, with a repeat, of strings in two cases, of a number and its text, lists of lists, objects whose member is a list, an object or a number, and an object against a number. The == case and its != twin together tell equal, not equal and a failed comparison apart. A positive control compares a list with itself. Controls first and last must answer true.",
